				1939,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Wind): Add polling loop for Tauri IPC bridge initialization\n\nThe `ResolveConfiguration` function previously assumed the Tauri IPC globals (`__TAURI_INTERNALS__` or `__TAURI__`) were immediately available. In certain webview load orderings or with the specific Mountain fork, these globals may be undefined during initial module evaluation, causing the configuration fetch to fail prematurely.\n\nIntroduce a 5-second polling loop with a 25ms interval that retries detection of the `Invoke` function. If the IPC bridge remains unavailable after the deadline, log a diagnostic message via `DevLog` and proceed with default path fallbacks. This ensures the workbench can boot in degraded mode rather than stalling indefinitely during initialization, while still attempting to recover native functionality if the bridge becomes ready shortly after start.\n\nThe update refactors the IPC resolution logic into a reusable `ResolveInvoke` helper and wraps the invocation with explicit TypeScript casting to satisfy the type checker.",
			"SHA": "ca4b721dc89fe3ab21da124d09dd57aa980c36db"
		},
